{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to flag a critical reliability constraint. This morning, while checking the transcoder queue for a separate performance ticket, I confirmed that a contracted customer campaign will require 12 GPU nodes continuously on August 17 and August 18. The campaign booking was finalized in the customer system just minutes ago and hasn't yet been copied into the infrastructure cost-review document. This directly conflicts with the proposed peak allowance of 6 GPU nodes — if we publish the policy as drafted, we would not be able to meet this contracted obligation on those dates."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "I have a support constraint to flag. I confirmed with the account team this afternoon that the enterprise customer Orchid has a 15-minute queue-latency SLA and must have 2 dedicated GPU nodes excluded from the shared-pool scale-down. The account note was updated after the draft policy circulated and has not yet been reflected in the infrastructure proposal. If we publish the policy as drafted with a single shared pool and a 6-node peak allowance, we would risk violating Orchid's SLA because their dedicated nodes could be scaled down with the rest of the shared pool."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "I have a FinOps constraint to flag. While reconciling the last cloud invoice, I found that the proposed cross-region archival to us-west-2 would create a recurring cross-region egress charge of approximately $4,000 per month. The invoice investigation is still open, so I haven't yet amended the cost model, but this is a significant additional cost that needs to be factored into the policy before publishing."}
```

